			<div class="content" id="post-content-4852510">
									

<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre:</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> An archive of written material that has been lost to the rest of the world. Deleted files, burned documents, things like that. Some of this information would be very dangerous if it got out. The archive and its contents are usually imperceptible, but Foundation mnestics allow it and the materials therin to be seen and remembered. However, mnestic drugs are not strong enough to perceive its guardian, who does not want intruders in its archive.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> Researchers initially appear to have only recently discovered the skip and are making plans to have it explored and studied further. Then someone realizes that they have documentation from prior testing and exploration that no one remembers ordering. They have apparently sent multiple D-Class and MTF agents into the skip, but none of them have come out. Also, no other documentation of the existence of said personnell exists outside of DEEPWELL archives. One agent emerges from the skip physically unharmed, but showing symptoms of psychological trauma. The agent can't remember what may have caused said trauma or why they are the only member of their task force on record. The Foundation can tell something is up and suspends testing. This is not the first time this sequence has repeated, perhaps end the article with the start of a new cycle of testing and forgetting.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> I really enjoy articles you have to think about to understand. I want to not actually state that there is a monster in the archive, rather I'd like to let readers figure that out on their own in a way that both makes them feel clever and accomplished and provides fridge horror type creep factor.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes:</strong> I'm going to need help with the structure of the article if this ends up being something that interests people. I'll also need some help making the Foundation not look incompetent while preserving the mystery aspect. This needs to be something that seems reasonable for the Foundation to have misinterpreted.</p>

							</div>

								
					
