<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Page Layout:</strong> Standard containment procedures and description, with background on its discovery. Interview and test logs showing how its anomalous effects were deduced, as well as further experimentation.</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong> A mattress/mattresses that induces vivid dreams in those who sleep in it. Upon waking up, their memories are retroactively altered to include, and frequently overridden with the contents of their dreams (e.g. a man who dreams of fishing may believe he had been a fisherman his whole life; a person who dreams of a deceased loved one believes they are still alive).</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong> A hospital gains Foundation attention after an outbreak of manic patients. Investigation leads to the discovery of the SCP. The affected patients are taken into Foundation custody to be examined so as to further understand the nature of the SCP.</p>
<p>The possibility of the SCP being used to treat treatment-resistant conditions is explored, leading to extensive testing. Humorous and dramatic attempts follow due to the SCP's unreliable nature.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber</strong>: It's a memory-altering SCP that relies on the user's dreams to fabricate memories.</p>
<p><strong>Additional Notes</strong>: I'm open to suggestions or developments to the concept and narrative.</p>

