<p><strong>Summoned via PM:</strong></p>
<p>Hi there Angryman22. Let’s take a look at your concept.</p>
<p>It starts off promising, but I’m struggling to connect the various anomalous together. For example, what does a survivor of a glass factory explosion have to do with “a strong hatred for transparent objects”? Furthermore, why is it that when they’re “exposed to even a very small amount of oxygen, they will engulf in flames reaching a temperature of 4000K”?</p>
<p>You appear to be adding these anomalous properties without consideration for purpose or reason. At best, this sounds like a possible body horror scip if you manage to delve deeper into the psychology of the humanoid. Tell us more about who Georgine Lass was/is. Why is she behaving the way she is after the explosion? At worst, however, this scip sounds like your typical Peter Parker-gets-bitten-by-a-radioactive-spider-and-becomes-a-superhero sort of story. Even then, you need to flesh out the character’s motivations and goals and tell us why she’s behaving as such.</p>
<p>If you decide to revise the concept / respond below, do drop me another PM and I’ll take another look. For now, all the best!</p>

