<p>Summoned via Pm<br />
Interesting SCP you've got there<br />
It would be a shame if someone&#8230;<br />
Critiqued it&#8230;</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>So while this idea has some potential, there are a LOT of things you need to fix before I (and many other concept reviewers) will consider giving you a greenlight.</p>
<ul>
<li>Elevator pitch: Don't tell me your idea isn't special. You're trying to sell me on the idea, so you need to be confident about it. Writing &quot;um this book isn't special&quot; is an immediate turn off. Try and find something unique. It doesn't have to be revolutionary or groundbreaking: just unique and intriguing enough to get someone to read through it.</li>
<li>Central Narrative: I'm sorry, but I barely understand the story you're going for. Where did the entity come from? Why did the serpent's hand ally with the Foundation? What brought SCP-1000 into the situation? You need to make your idea more concise. It's barely half baked right now: mising al the details that a successful article has. You honestly need to work on your idea before moving forward.</li>
<li>Hook: You need more than just a pair of O5s to get your story to appear interesting. Tel me why I should read your article rather than another article. Also, where did Merlin come from?</li>
<li>Additional Notes: This idea needs to go back in the oven IT's lacking the crucial components and skill necessary for creating a coherent and compelling piece. This idea is salvageable, but you need to really work on your writing skills. Apologies if anything here sounded rude, as that was not my intent.</li>
</ul>
</div>
</div>
</div>

