<p><strong>Seeking Greenlights:</strong> Yes</p>
<p><strong>Page Type:</strong> SCP Article</p>
<p><strong>Genre (Optional):</strong> Horror</p>
<p><strong>Elevator Pitch:</strong></p>
<p>A humanoid figure looking like a starving man.<br />
Any human who goes near it that laughs gets attacked, bitten/ripped, and peeled by the SCP.<br />
He's locked in a simple windowless room.</p>
<p><strong>Central Narrative:</strong></p>
<p>Starts off in urban Florida 2019, where the SCP was presumed to be a homeless man living on the street.<br />
It was there for 2 years, not doing anything until it was caught trying to peel (with teeth) a local teen's skin off.<br />
Video footage was captured (eventually uploaded online), and the SCP quickly-crawled away with the body.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;show&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Foundation field agents were warned and investigated after widespread local fear of SCP-XXXX online.<br />
MTF Search-Teams found SCP-XXXX by an urban lake.<br />
SCP's didn't eat, breathe, talk or scream, and walked on all fours similar to a spider.<br />
It was captured by MTF. (Audio Attached)</p>
<p>Foundation put coverup stories, making a fake background, court charges, and sentencing.<br />
Foundation took a list of items where SCP was recorded: Printed photos of people of ranging ages and an old coat SCP wore made of skin parts of different animals.</p>
<p>Research on the photos (attached) revealed the people were that of now-dead people.<br />
People were that of children, adults, prison inmates, and one of the leading researchers of the Foundation.<br />
Connections between lists of people could not be found by staff, but details of who they are, are given.<br />
Hidden letters on the photos revealed words &quot;fam&quot;, &quot;peel&quot;, &quot;ric&quot;, &quot;sorrow&quot;, &quot;controlling&quot;, &quot;it's gone&quot;, and &quot;give it back&quot;.<br />
A note was found in the coat that stated &quot;Life is given to those with lemons, a bad one is given to those with oranges&quot;.</p>
<p>D-class was used to experiment on the SCP, audio recordings, and experiment chart was attached.<br />
SCP-XXXX didn't react or attack until the third experiment, where the D-Class chuckled nervously.<br />
More experiments occurred until Foundation found out SCP-XXXX only reacts to D-class laughing at certain distances.</p>
<p>SCP-XXXX was watched over after every kill, in which he was seen to make shapes with the pieces of skin.<br />
Foundation gave SCP-XXXX crayons and paper, but it only used skin to make shapes.<br />
Recreated drawings were made (and attached), with the most identifiable ones as an orange, a house, a frowning face, and a knife.</p>
<p><strong>Hook/Attention-Grabber:</strong> Creepiness is from lack of info on the lore.</p>
